    {
      "id": "GENUS_PROTRELLETA",
      "name": "Protrelleta",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Protrelleta — a genus of chromadoreas.",
      "lineage": "Protrelleta",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "SP_PROTRELLETA_FLORIDANA_CHITWOOD_1932",
          "name": "Protrelleta floridana Chitwood, 1932",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Protrelleta",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Female. Body comparatively long and slender, widening gradually posterior to head, towards the level of the vulva, reaching its maximum width at level of the joint of the anterior and posterior uteri, then narrowing gradually towards tail. Cervical cuticle unarmed, markedly annulated from the base of the head to the level of the excretory pore. Lateral alae absent. Head comparatively long, conical, truncate. Oral opening surrounded by eight lips formed by curled cuticle, arranged as two sub-dorsal, two sub-ventral and four sub-lateral structures. Head bearing eight long digitiform cephalic papillae (their length ca. 4 µm) arising from the external edge of the lips. Each cephalic papilla corresponding to one lip. Stoma similar in length to the head, ca. same diameter of the anterior end of the corpus. Oesophagus consisting of a muscular, cylindrical corpus, with a dilation or pseudobulb at level of the vulva, then diminishing its diameter toward the isthmus where it has a similar diameter to its anterior part. Isthmus cylindrical, its diameter similar to that of the base of the corpus. Basal bulb spherical, valve-plate well-developed. Intestine simple, sub-rectilinear. Rectum comparatively long. Anus prominent. Nerve ring encircling corpus at ca. 40 % of its length. Excretory pore ventral, in the region of the corpus, just anterior to the vulva.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:7031670"
        },
